Here's a complete implementation:

**In `Program.cs` — configure size limits and add the endpoint:**

```csharp
// Configure form options to enforce the 10 MB limit
builder.Services.Configure<FormOptions>(options =>
{
    options.MultipartBodyLengthLimit = 10 * 1024 * 1024; // 10 MB
});

// If using Kestrel, also set the request body size limit
builder.WebHost.ConfigureKestrel(options =>
{
    options.Limits.MaxRequestBodySize = 10 * 1024 * 1024;
});

var app = builder.Build();

// ... existing middleware including app.UseAntiforgery() ...

app.MapPost("/upload", async (IFormFile file) =>
{
    if (file.Length == 0)
        return Results.BadRequest("Empty file.");

    if (file.Length > 10 * 1024 * 1024)
        return Results.BadRequest("File exceeds 10 MB limit.");

    var allowedTypes = new[] { "image/jpeg", "image/png" };
    if (!allowedTypes.Contains(file.ContentType, StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
        return Results.BadRequest("Only JPEG and PNG files are allowed.");

    var allowedExtensions = new[] { ".jpg", ".jpeg", ".png" };
    var ext = Path.GetExtension(file.FileName).ToLowerInvariant();
    if (!allowedExtensions.Contains(ext))
        return Results.BadRequest("Invalid file extension.");

    var uploadsDir = Path.Combine(Directory.GetCurrentDirectory(), "uploads");
    Directory.CreateDirectory(uploadsDir);

    // Use a random name to avoid collisions and path traversal
    var savedName = $"{Guid.NewGuid()}{ext}";
    var filePath = Path.Combine(uploadsDir, savedName);

    await using var stream = new FileStream(filePath, FileMode.Create);
    await file.CopyToAsync(stream);

    return Results.Ok(new { fileName = savedName });
})
.DisableAntiforgery()      // remove this line if you ARE sending the antiforgery token
.DisableRequestSizeLimit(); // optional: let FormOptions be the sole enforcer
```

**Key points:**

- **Two-layer size limit** — Kestrel rejects oversized bodies before buffering; `FormOptions` enforces it at the form-parsing level.
- **Content-type + extension check** — validates both to prevent trivial spoofing.
- **`Guid` filename** — avoids path-traversal attacks and name collisions.
- **`DisableAntiforgery()`** — needed if callers (e.g. mobile/SPA) won't send the token. Remove it if your form sends the antiforgery token.
